meta {
  name: Create device
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{restartersBase}}/api/v2/devices?api_token={{process.env.RESTARTERS_TOKEN}}
  body: multipartForm
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  api_token: {{process.env.RESTARTERS_TOKEN}}
}

body:multipart-form {
  eventid: {{restartersEventId}}
  category: 16
  item_type: Laptop
  brand: Dell
  model: Inspiron 15
  problem: Would not power on, charging light flashed yellow twice. Replaced faulty DC power jack soldered onto the motherboard.
  notes: Owner said it stopped charging after the cable was yanked out.
  age: 6
  spare_parts: Third party
  repair_status: Fixed
}

docs {
  Writes to live Restarters data. Use a test event.
  
  Required: category, item_type. category ids are listed in docs/restarters_api/README.md.
  There is no repair_details field. "problem" holds both the problem and the fix.
  Response is { id, device, stats }, not { data } as the spec says. Copy the top-level id into restartersDeviceId in the dev environment.
  age: years, approximate is fine. 0 means unknown.
  spare_parts: No / Manufacturer / Third party. The spec says Repairable only. This request tests it on a Fixed item.
  next_steps only applies when repair_status is Repairable.
  barrier only applies when repair_status is End of life.
}
